<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>DON'T MESS DIRECTLY WITH THE WINDOWS FILES. USE A F=
ILE COPY.</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Windows 10/11 builds use MUN files for storing ressources i=
n Windows SystemRessources folder.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>C:\Windows\System32\</code> DLL files link to MUN fil=
es in <code>C:\Windows\SystemResources\</code> with .mun added at the end.<=
/p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Use archive extractor like 7zip to extract the MUN files co=
ntent like images and icons.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">If you want images and icons check <code>.rsrc\ICON</code> =
once extracted.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">They are still png and icons but, have no file extension an=
d are named with numbers</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Rename them to correct file extension to let Windows know h=
ow to open them.</p>
